-- title:
--   RFC 7748 §5.2 — the two X25519 test vectors
-- statement:
--   The function `x25519` of bundle `X25519Dalek_Rfc7748` gives the outputs RFC 7748 lists for its two X25519 test vectors: for the 32-byte scalars `a546e36b…449ac4` and `4b66e9d4…18ba0d` and the 32-byte $u$-coordinates `e6db6867…ab1c4c` and `e5210f12…15a493`, the outputs are `c3da5537…a28552` and `95cbde94…ac7957` (all bytes as in the RFC, in order, written out in full in the statement).
--
--   RFC 7748, §5.2: “Two types of tests are provided. The first is a pair of test vectors for each function that consist of expected outputs for the given inputs. The inputs are generally given as 64 or 112 hexadecimal digits that need to be decoded as 32 or 56 binary bytes before processing.”
-- source:
--   A. Langley, M. Hamburg and S. Turner, Elliptic Curves for Security, RFC 7748, January 2016, https://doi.org/10.17487/RFC7748, §5.2, the X25519 test vectors (p. 5 of the excerpts)

